              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Malayalam for a hero, then the Malayalam for a moral."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: പ്രേതം",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പ്രേതം — prētaṁ — \"a ghost\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ആ പഴയ വീട്ടിൽ ഒരു പ്രേതം ഉണ്ടെന്ന് ആളുകൾ പറയുന്നു. ā paḻaya vīṭṭil oru prētaṁ uṇṭennŭ āḷukaḷ paṟayunnu. People say there is a ghost in that old house."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A story word; people tell ghost stories, പ്രേതകഥകൾ, at night."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പ്രേതം (prētaṁ) is borrowed from Sanskrit preta, \"departed, dead; the spirit of a dead person\" (Monier-Williams)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
